  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 1980s, after Reagan became president, a man named Bill Sweetman took a deep look at special access programs, or SAPs: highly restricted classified projects that are kept walled off from one another. What he looked at was how these programs were split into compartments and how some of them duplicated each other. A guest named Eric W. Davis brings this up to Michels from memory, hedging that he thinks it was Sweetman, during a talk about whether a US president was briefed on UFOs."
}
